Step 1 — Export Gerber dari KiCad dulu
Di KiCad PCB Editor:
File → Plot
Format: Gerber
Centang layer: F.Cu dan Edge.Cuts
Klik Plot
Klik Generate Drill Files → Generate Drill File
Klik Close

Step 2 — Import ke FlatCAM
Buka FlatCAM:
File → Open Gerber → pilih sensor_tanah-F_Cu.gbr
File → Open Gerber lagi → pilih sensor_tanah-Edge_Cuts.gbr
File → Open Excellon → pilih sensor_tanah-PTH.drl

Step 3 — Buat Jalur Milling (Routing Job)
Klik file F_Cu.gbr di panel kiri
Klik tab Isolation Tool
Setting:
Tool dia: 0.1mm
Pass: 1
Klik Generate Geometry
Klik geometry yang muncul di panel kiri
Tab Properties → scroll bawah
Setting:
Cut Z: -0.1
Travel Z: 2.0
Feedrate X-Y: 120
Feedrate Z: 60
Klik Generate CNCJob object
Screenshot tampilan ini → SS Jalur Milling ✅
Klik Save CNC Code → simpan file .gcode

Step 4 — Buat Titik Drilling
Klik file PTH.drl di panel kiri
Tab Properties → klik Drilling Tool
Centang semua tool
Setting:
Cut Z: -1.7
Travel Z: 2.0
Klik Generate CNCJob object
Screenshot tampilan ini → SS Titik Drilling ✅
Klik Save CNC Code → simpan file .gcode drill

Save G-Code Milling
Klik sensor_tanah-F_Cu.gbr_iso_combin... di panel kiri (bagian CNC Job)
Tab Properties
Scroll bawah → klik Save CNC Code
Simpan dengan nama milling.gcode

Save G-Code Drilling
Klik sensor_tanah-PTH.drl_cnc di panel kiri
Tab Properties
Scroll bawah → klik Save CNC Code
Simpan dengan nama drilling.gcode
